[Music]  I'm Keith Olbermann and this is the  resistance you may not know the  difference between the Pittsburgh  Penguins and the Penguins from Batman  and the only thing Donald Trump may know  about them is that they play a sport  where one of the positions is called  right wing but at this moment they are  or nearly are the centerpieces in the  lack of culture war between America's  would-be dictator and those of us who  you know like democracy the Penguins  have mastered this continents most  grueling and demanding sports season and  have won the greatest trophy in sports  the Stanley Cup in back-to-back years  but right now they have in fact become  the Pittsburgh political pawns  last Saturday apparently having just  learned that the basketball champion  Golden State Warriors had refused to go  to the inevitably painful but by now  traditional White House Championship  photo-op Trump pretended he was refusing  to see them exactly 26 hours later the  Penguins tweeted out a link to a  statement about their planned visit to  the White House to what used to be the  symbol of American democracy until Trump  came along the Pittsburgh Penguins  respect the institution of the office of  the president and the long tradition of  championship teams visiting the White  House we attended White House ceremonies  after previous championships touring the  historic building and visiting briefly  with President George HW Bush and Barack  Obama and have accepted an invitation to  attend again this year any agreement or  disagreement with the president's  politics policies or agenda can be  expressed in other ways however we very  much respect the rights of other  individuals and groups to express  themselves as they see fit as an ardent  hockey fan whose mother saw the New York  Rangers win a game in the Stanley Cup  final of 1940 and who laments the sports  relative obscurity here and who has for  50 years  found among hockey people some of the  most naturally understanding and  inclusive and empathetic of all people I  know what the Penguins were trying to do  here among other things they might be  going to the White House as soon as  October 11th so they were trying to get  out in front of trouble but anybody with  a little more sophistication could have  told them what would necessarily happen  next  Trump panicking over the instantaneous  repudiation  his National Football League boycott  idea in at least two cases by his  buddies Bob Kraft and Schad Kahn NFL  owners who had reportedly donated  millions to his inauguration committee  Trump looking for a fight after the  warriors humiliated him picked up the  Penguins sweet little gesture of a note  and began to hit people over the head  with it pleased to inform that the  champion Pittsburgh Penguins of the NHL  will be joining me at the White House  for ceremony great team first of all  it's pleased with addy [ __ ] secondly  the Penguins are now Trump's political  pawns they're nice little apolitical  excuse us most of us are Canadian any  agreement or disagreement with the  president's politics policies or agenda  can be expressed in other ways statement  that has been erased there are now  political pawns the Pittsburgh political  pawns their trip to the White House is  now agreement not disagreement with this  president's politics policies and agenda  his hatreds are now the Penguins hatreds  his racism's are now the Penguins  racism's his lunacies are now the  Penguins lunacies but it's worse than  that  at the start of the month the National  Hockey League and its players union made  a big deal out of something new called  hockey's Declaration of Principles it is  all good stuff about ideals and  character and life skills and there's  nothing about just keep your stick on  the puck and don't get down on your luck  and then there's the last of the  principles number eight all hockey  programs should provide a safe positive  and inclusive environment for players  and families regardless of race color  religion national origin gender age  disability sexual orientation and  socioeconomic status simply put hockey  is for everyone Bravo unfortunately  Penguins Donald Trump is not for  everyone if there were ever a time you  do not want to go see this guy it's when  your entire sport has just stood up for  inclusion and against discrimination for  race color religion national origin or  anything else and the President of the  United States has just described a bunch  of African American athletes by  screaming quote get that son of a [ __ ]  off  the field right now out he's fired is  fired the Penguins are captained by  Sidney Crosby and owned by a former star  player named Mario Lemieux and the two  of them are legendary for their  leadership and neither Crosby nor  Lemieux is showing any leadership right  now nor is the National Hockey League  nor its commissioner Gary Bettman the  Penguins can't go I don't care if they  have to claim they can't find the  Stanley Cup and they will show up when  and if they locate it I don't care if  they say the coach has cancelled the  trip and demanded a 16-hour practice  instead that day  NHL coaches are always doing something  like that anyway the Pittsburgh Penguins  must now decline the white house  invitation or render hockey's new  Declaration of Principles laughingly  meaningless there's nothing in there  about athletes being used by a crazy  political figure in a desperate crisis  of his own making and being paraded out  in front of a camera like they are all  Dennis Rodman visiting Kim jong-un  there's nothing in there about  politeness and the hockey desire to  please everybody that requires you to  become political hostages or the  Pittsburgh political props or the  Pittsburgh political pawns or the  Pittsburgh PAC seized resist remove  piece

